text.section:
When the affairs of a business trust have been wound up pursuant to § 13.1-1236, it shall file articles of cancellation with the Commission. The articles shall set forth:

The name of the business trust;


The identification number issued by the Commission to the business trust;


The effective date of its certificate of trust;


A statement that the business trust has completed the winding up of its affairs; and


Any other information the trustees determine to include therein, including the reason for filing the articles of cancellation.
